@@ -0,0 +1,133 @@
+# Renewals
+
+## Why
+
+Members often want to keep a book longer. Today staff do this by returning the
+copy and checking it out again, which closes one loan and opens another and
+breaks the member's loan history. A renewal extends the open loan in place: same
+loan, a later due date, and a count of how many times it was renewed.
+
+## Interface (fixed; other code calls exactly this)
+
+- `LendingService.renew(loan_id: str) -> Loan` in `src/lending/service.py` — renews the open loan in
+  place (same `loan_id`) and returns it.
+- `Loan` in `src/lending/models.py` gets a field `renewals: int` (default `0`): how many times the
+  loan has been renewed.
+- Add `RenewalRefused(LendingError)` to `src/lending/errors.py` for renewals that can't be granted;
+  unknown loan ids keep raising `LoanNotFound`, and keep using the other existing error classes where
+  they already fit.
+
+## Rules
+
+**Settled earlier, carried over from the previous spec as written:**
+
+> - **Renewals:** renewing an overdue loan charges the fine accrued so far, as if
+>   the copy were returned on the renewal day, with the same rates, cap and child
+>   exemption. After the renewal, lateness counts against the new due date.
+>   Lateness before a renewal must never just disappear.
+> - **Renewals and holds:** a loan can't be renewed while anyone is still `WAITING`
+>   in the queue for its title. A `READY` hold doesn't count, because that member
+>   already has their copy.
+> - **Renewals and money:** only members who are paid up can renew. If the
+>   balance shows anything owed when they ask, they can't renew until they've
+>   paid.
+
+**What a renewal is.** The loan stays the same loan: same `loan_id`, `copy_id`,
+member and `borrowed_on`, and the copy stays `ON_LOAN`. The renewal gives the
+loan a new `due_on` and adds one to `renewals`.
+
+**New due date.** A fresh full loan period counted from the renewal day, exactly
+like a checkout made that day. If it lands on a Sunday, it moves to the Monday.
+
+**What can be renewed.** A loan can be renewed only if all of these hold:
+- It is open (not returned).
+- Its copy is a book. DVDs are never renewable.
+- It has been renewed fewer than 2 times.
+- Today is no earlier than 5 calendar days before its current `due_on`. There is
+  no upper cutoff, so overdue loans can be renewed.
+- No hold on its title is `WAITING`.
+- The member's balance, taken when they ask and before any fine this renewal
+  would charge, is zero.
+
+A renewal that owes money is refused with `AccountBlocked`. Every other refusal
+above is `RenewalRefused`. An unknown loan id is `LoanNotFound`.
+
+**Refusals change nothing.** A refused renewal leaves the due date, the renewal
+count and the account as they were. It uses up nothing.
+
+**Not a new loan.** The loan limit doesn't apply, and a member at their limit
+can renew.
+
+## Acceptance criteria
+
+Fixtures: Monday 2 March 2026 is the start day. Adult `ann`, child `kid`, and
+further adults as needed. Book `978-1` (replacement 18.00) has copies `B1` and
+`B2`. DVD `dvd-1` has the single copy `D1`. A book checked out on 2 March is due
+Monday 23 March.
+
+Granting
+1. A new loan has `renewals == 0`.
+2. `renew` returns the same loan: same `loan_id`, `copy_id`, `member_id` and
+   `borrowed_on`, with `renewals == 1`. `get_loan` shows the same values, and
+   the copy is still `ON_LOAN`.
+3. A book due Mon 23 March and renewed Thu 19 March is due Thu 9 April.
+4. A book renewed on Sunday 22 March (+21 days is Sunday 12 April) is due
+   Monday 13 April.
+5. The renewal does not add a loan. `open_loans` and `loan_history` still show
+   one loan for that copy.
+6. A member at their loan limit can renew.
+
+Timing
+7. A book due Mon 23 March can be renewed on Wed 18 March. On Tue 17 March,
+   `renew` raises `RenewalRefused`.
+8. The window follows the current due date. After a renewal on 18 March (now due
+   Wed 8 April), a second renewal is refused on Thu 2 April and granted on Fri
+   3 April.
+
+Limits
+9. A loan can be renewed twice. The third `renew` raises `RenewalRefused` and
+   `renewals` stays 2.
+10. `renew` on a DVD loan raises `RenewalRefused`.
+11. `renew` on a returned loan raises `RenewalRefused`.
+12. `renew` raises `LoanNotFound` for an unknown loan id.
+
+Holds
+13. While another member has a `WAITING` hold on the loan's title, `renew` raises
+    `RenewalRefused`.
+14. Once that hold is no longer waiting (for example, cancelled), the loan can be
+    renewed.
+15. A `READY` hold on the title, with nobody `WAITING`, does not stop the renewal.
+
+Money
+16. A member whose balance is 0.01 or more gets `AccountBlocked` from `renew`.
+17. After paying the balance off, the same member can renew.
+
+Overdue renewals
+18. An adult's book due Mon 23 March and renewed Wed 25 March is granted. It
+    charges a 0.50 fine for that loan (two open days) and is due Wed 15 April.
+19. Returning that loan on Wed 15 April charges nothing more. Returning it on Fri
+    17 April charges 0.50 more, counted against 15 April.
+20. A child's overdue renewal charges nothing.
+21. The replacement-cost cap covers the renewal fine and later fines together.
+    For a book with replacement cost 1.00, a renewal 6 open days late charges
+    1.00. A later late return charges nothing more.
+22. A fine posted by an overdue renewal is owed, so the next renewal raises
+    `AccountBlocked` until it is paid.
+23. After an overdue renewal, the loan is not in `overdue_loans` again until
+    after its new due date.
+
+Refusals
+24. Each refused renewal (criteria 7, 9–11, 13 and 16) leaves `due_on`,
+    `renewals` and the member's balance unchanged.
+
+Unchanged behaviour
+25. The existing test suite still passes.
+
+## Non-goals
+
+- A list or log of individual renewals. The count is the only record.
+- Member self-service or online renewal.
+- Renewal reminders or notices.
+- Automatic renewal.
+- Different renewal limits for children or for particular titles.
+- Changes to `overdue_report` beyond what follows from `due_on` moving.
